  "caption": "Quinn reached for the top-shelf biscuits and got a sharp shoulder pain out of nowhere — and nights were even grumpier. The X-ray showed a calcium deposit in a rotator cuff tendon.\n\nThese deposits can be completely silent or quite painful, often during the phase when the body is breaking them down. And no, calcium in your diet isn't the cause.\n\nWhat can help: gentle movement within comfort during a flare, rebuilding cuff strength with tolerable loading, and easing back into daily tasks gradually. If it persists, discuss a specialist review with your GP.\n\nGet it checked if pain follows a fall or knock, or there's fever, unexplained weakness, a change in shape, or chest symptoms.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
